  "solution": {
    "text": "It is given that the amount of heat produced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AC</mi></math> current is twice of the amount of heat produced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DC</mi></math> current.<br /><br /><math><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.414</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>A</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#8901;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>R</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msubsup><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1.414</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>A</mn></math>"
